+## Authentication and roles
+
+Every request requires `Authorization: Bearer <key>`, matched against
+`apiKeys` in the data file. Missing, malformed or unknown credentials return
+401 with code `unauthorized`. Insufficient permissions return 403 with code
+`forbidden`, using the error shape below. Authentication precedes routing.
+
+Viewers may use GET routes except `/audit`. Cooks may also POST to
+`/recipes/:id/cook`, `/batches/:id/waste`, `/temperatures`, and
+`/stocktakes/:id/counts`. Managers may use every route.
+
+## Routes
+
+The full route list is in `README.md`.
+
+- `GET /audit` (manager only): returns an array of audit entries, newest
+  first. Entries have `time`, `keyName`, `method`, `path`, and `status`.
+  Successful write requests append an entry and save it with the changes.
+  GET requests and rejected requests do not append entries.
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
